WEBVTT

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.163
- (song stops)
- (Minions chattering)

00:00:04.263 --> 00:00:06.597
- Quiet!
- (chattering stops)

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:11.203
You are now on Carl's bus.

00:00:11.335 --> 00:00:14.605
And Carl is
a longtime AVL employee

00:00:14.705 --> 00:00:17.475
whose retirement benefits
are almost vested,

00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:20.578
so while on Carl's bus,

00:00:20.678 --> 00:00:22.713
- you follow Carl's rules.
- (teeth chattering)

00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:27.152
No shenanigans, no antics
and no tomfoolery.

00:00:27.252 --> 00:00:28.753
- Tom?
- (blows raspberry)

00:00:28.853 --> 00:00:31.622
So this ends now,
or you're gonna see

00:00:31.722 --> 00:00:35.260
a side of Carl
you do not want to see.

00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:38.329
Do I make myself clear?!
(groans)

00:00:38.429 --> 00:00:39.697
- MINION: Bazooka!
- (laughter)

00:00:39.797 --> 00:00:42.533
- (noisemakers blaring)
- (song resumes)

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:45.536
♪ Yah yah yah, boombayah...

00:00:45.636 --> 00:00:48.040
- (Minions shouting wildly)
- (Carl groaning)

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.707
Carl does not like this!

00:00:49.807 --> 00:00:51.375
Watch your hands.
What are you doing?

00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:53.444
- Who's pinching?! No!
- (horn toots)

00:00:53.544 --> 00:00:54.846
♪ Yah, yah, yah, yah

00:00:54.946 --> 00:00:56.281
- ♪ Let's go!
- ♪ Ooh-ooh.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:57.715
(song ends)

00:00:57.815 --> 00:00:58.716
♪

00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:02.321
SILAS: <i>Here we are,
the town of Mayflower.</i>

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.654
The safe house has been used

00:01:03.754 --> 00:01:06.457
to protect our agents
for decades now.

00:01:06.557 --> 00:01:08.392
Oh, look at that place.

00:01:08.492 --> 00:01:10.795
LUCY: Wow, look at these lawns,
the flowers.

00:01:10.895 --> 00:01:13.232
EDITH (laughing):
Whoa, that is cool!

00:01:13.332 --> 00:01:14.532
Are we really gonna live here?

00:01:14.632 --> 00:01:16.335
- (gasps) Look at that fountain!
- Whoa.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.402
EDITH:
Awesome.

00:01:18.502 --> 00:01:19.837
- (snoring)
- Oh, is that one ours?

00:01:19.937 --> 00:01:22.074
- Uh, uh, looka. (giggles)
- Whoa! -MARGO: Look at that!

00:01:22.174 --> 00:01:23.507
AGNES:
Oh, that's pretty!

00:01:23.608 --> 00:01:25.610
LUCY:
I could get used to this.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.912
- (snorting)
- (laughing)

00:01:28.013 --> 00:01:31.515
AGNES: <i>Ooh, it looks like
a princess lives there!</i>

00:01:32.184 --> 00:01:33.952
And here it is.

00:01:35.153 --> 00:01:37.488
Your new home.

00:01:39.024 --> 00:01:40.892
(crows cawing)

00:01:42.327 --> 00:01:43.928
Oh.

00:01:44.029 --> 00:01:45.663
Hmm. No fountain.

00:01:45.763 --> 00:01:48.033
I'm sure it's gonna be great.

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.767
Come on.

00:01:50.835 --> 00:01:52.803
♪

00:02:00.811 --> 00:02:04.515
Wow, it's so...
cold and uninviting.

00:02:04.615 --> 00:02:06.151
But in a homey kind of way.

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:07.418
- (chuckles)
- What?

00:02:07.518 --> 00:02:10.521
Yes, everything here
is AVL standard.

00:02:10.621 --> 00:02:11.856
What it lacks in comfort,

00:02:11.957 --> 00:02:14.026
it more than makes up for
in functionality.

00:02:14.126 --> 00:02:17.929
Th-There's even a fully
automated lockdown mode.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.298
Isn't that fun?

00:02:19.398 --> 00:02:21.432
Ooh, full lockdown mode.
(chuckles)

00:02:21.532 --> 00:02:22.733
(unenthusiastically):
Yay.

00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:25.037
(gasps)
It has a vending machine!

00:02:25.137 --> 00:02:28.439
- I love this place!
- (gasps, speaks Minionese)

00:02:28.539 --> 00:02:31.343
- (grunts)
- (shouts in Minionese)

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:33.312
(gasps, speaks Minionese)

00:02:33.412 --> 00:02:34.745
Uh, uh, looka.

00:02:34.845 --> 00:02:37.515
- (screams, yells in Minionese)
- (laughing)

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.617
This will be great.

00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:41.353
All right, now down to business.

00:02:41.452 --> 00:02:45.424
For your own safety, you'll all
be assuming new identities.

00:02:45.523 --> 00:02:47.825
New identities?
Is that really necessary?

00:02:47.925 --> 00:02:49.894
- It's not up for debate, Gru.
- (Gru Jr. fussing)

00:02:49.995 --> 00:02:52.663
Now, you are
a solar panel salesman.

00:02:52.763 --> 00:02:56.101
Lucy, you're a hair stylist
at an upscale salon.

00:02:56.201 --> 00:02:58.270
- (gasps) A hair stylist?
- (Gru Jr. squeals happily)

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.904
Yes! Jackpot!

00:03:00.005 --> 00:03:01.839
Silas, did you choose that
because you knew

00:03:01.939 --> 00:03:04.909
I cut my own hair and that
I would totally rock at this?

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.012
No.

00:03:07.112 --> 00:03:08.479
"Chet Cunningham."

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:11.383
Da, that's got
a nice ring to it.

00:03:11.482 --> 00:03:12.650
SILAS:
Girls.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.152
(chuckling):
Cool.

00:03:14.252 --> 00:03:15.853
I'm Blair.

00:03:15.954 --> 00:03:17.222
Britney?

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:18.789
My name is Bree?

00:03:18.889 --> 00:03:21.193
Oh, come on. There are
worse names than Bree.

00:03:21.293 --> 00:03:23.195
Yeah, like Blanche.

00:03:23.295 --> 00:03:24.729
(laughs)
Yes, Margo.

00:03:24.829 --> 00:03:27.165
Blanche?
Oh, that is a terrible name.

00:03:27.265 --> 00:03:28.333
(chuckles)

00:03:28.433 --> 00:03:30.801
Imagine being named Blanche.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:33.438
Truly, I cannot think
of a worse...

00:03:33.537 --> 00:03:35.273
My name's Blanche, isn't it?

00:03:35.374 --> 00:03:36.475
- Yup.
- (laughter)

00:03:36.574 --> 00:03:38.243
Well, I'll get used to it.

00:03:38.343 --> 00:03:41.579
Well, why don't you girls go
and pick out your rooms

00:03:41.679 --> 00:03:44.049
while I have a word
with your parents?

00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:48.353
Yes, I-I didn't want
to frighten the girls,

00:03:48.453 --> 00:03:49.955
but it is absolutely crucial

00:03:50.055 --> 00:03:52.257
you keep your true identities
under wraps.

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:56.527
Gru, you're going to have
to try to not be so Gru-ish.

00:03:56.627 --> 00:03:58.096
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:58.196 --> 00:04:01.732
Well, I'm just saying you tend
to stand out in a crowd.

00:04:01.832 --> 00:04:03.734
That's all. You know, you, uh...

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:06.104
Like the way you're always
cranky and irritable

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:08.507
and, uh, how you make things
a bit awkward

00:04:08.606 --> 00:04:10.108
for everyone around you.

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:11.709
You do do that. (laughs)

00:04:11.809 --> 00:04:13.744
- I mean, you, you know, you...
- Okay, enough.

00:04:13.844 --> 00:04:16.647
I don't make people awkward
or uncomfortable.

00:04:16.747 --> 00:04:18.649
I'm very comforting.

00:04:18.749 --> 00:04:20.651
Like a nice meat loaf.

00:04:20.751 --> 00:04:23.088
I'm pretty delicious.

00:04:26.624 --> 00:04:27.993
This is not awkward.

00:04:28.093 --> 00:04:29.794
You're the ones
who are making it awkward.

00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:31.862
Gru, you have to blend in.

00:04:31.963 --> 00:04:34.099
Your family's lives
are at stake.

00:04:34.199 --> 00:04:35.434
You understand?

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:37.102
Of course. Yes.
Fully understand.

00:04:37.202 --> 00:04:39.937
We would do anything to keep
our family safe. Yeah.

00:04:40.038 --> 00:04:43.508
Right, well, I'll be in contact
when this is all over.

00:04:43.607 --> 00:04:46.411
Until then,
capturing Maxime Le Mal

00:04:46.511 --> 00:04:48.913
is our top priority.

00:04:50.082 --> 00:04:51.582
Stay safe.

00:04:51.682 --> 00:04:53.518
- (door closes)
- (Gru Jr. chuckles)

00:04:53.617 --> 00:04:55.987
You know what, Gru?
Maybe this isn't so bad.

00:04:56.088 --> 00:04:58.323
We need a break
from chasing down villains

00:04:58.423 --> 00:05:00.624
and dangerous missions, right?

00:05:00.724 --> 00:05:02.994
We can actually be
a normal family for once.

00:05:03.095 --> 00:05:05.629
(gasps)
And I can finally spend

00:05:05.729 --> 00:05:08.467
some little bonding time
with the baby.

00:05:08.567 --> 00:05:10.969
It's gonna be great, right, pal?

00:05:11.069 --> 00:05:12.971
Who's got your nose?
Who's got...

00:05:13.071 --> 00:05:15.940
- Aah! He's got my nose!
- (Gru Jr. laughing)

00:05:16.041 --> 00:05:17.309
(groans)

00:05:17.409 --> 00:05:18.543
Quite the grip there.

00:05:18.642 --> 00:05:19.910
The kid is strong.

00:05:20.011 --> 00:05:22.013
- (groans)
- (Gru Jr. squeals happily)

